{"code":"E15","wikidata":"Q13021846","wikipedia":{"en":"Samrong station","th":"สถานีสำโรง"},"summary":{"en":"Samrong is the name of two connecting rapid transit stations, on the Sukhumvit Line of the BTS Skytrain and the MRT Yellow Line, in Samut Prakan, Thailand. Trial operations on the BTS began in March 2017, and the station was officially opened by Prime Minister Prayut Chan-o-cha on 3 April 2017, with passengers able to ride the extension for free for a month beginning on 4 April 2017. It was the eastern terminus of the line, until the opening of the other stations of the Sukhumvit Line Extension (East) on 6 December 2018.","th":"สถานีสำโรง เป็นสถานีรถไฟฟ้าในอำเภอเมืองสมุทรปราการ จังหวัดสมุทรปราการ ในเส้นทาง"},"opened":"2017-04-03","photos":[{"thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/BTS_Samrong_station.jpg/960px-BTS_Samrong_station.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BTS_Samrong_station.jpg","author":"Sirakorn Lamyai","license":"CC0"},{"thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/BTS_Samrong_01.jpg/960px-BTS_Samrong_01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BTS_Samrong_01.jpg","author":"Oum13928","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/BTS_Samrong_stn._%281%29.jpg/960px-BTS_Samrong_stn._%281%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BTS_Samrong_stn._(1).jpg","author":"暇・カキコ","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/BTS_Samrong_stn._%282%29.jpg/960px-BTS_Samrong_stn._%282%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BTS_Samrong_stn._(2).jpg","author":"暇